model {
  extend basalt.build {
    metadata {
      constraint "The managed test Cloud's Worker logs in to its disposable database as a runtime role shaped like production's: it inherits read-all and write-all data, owns no objects, is not a superuser and may not create in the public schema. Migrations and test fixtures keep the schema owner. Every disposable database, a cloned target included, creates that role first so it keeps one catalog identity, so a runtime query that needs schema ownership fails in the scenarios. Cloning and production-operation fixtures keep their owner connection separate from the Worker's runtime-role URL, including while test scopes replace runtime bindings."
    }
  }
}
